# Generated from the OSRS Wiki page "Transcript:Prince Ali Rescue" by tools/quests/transcript_to_dialogue.py
0	section	Starting out
0	section	Talking to Chancellor Hassan
1	line	Chancellor Hassan	Greetings! I am Hassan, Chancellor to the Emir of Al Kharid.
1	option	Is there anything I can help you with?
2	line	Player	Is there anything I can help you with?
2	line	Chancellor Hassan	Well... we do currently have a very urgent issue we need to resolve, and I suppose you look like someone who knows how to get a job done. Are you definitely interested in helping?
2	select	Start the Prince Ali Rescue quest?
2	option	Yes.
3	line	Player	Of course.
3	line	Chancellor Hassan	You'll find our Spymaster, Osman, just outside the palace. Go to him and tell him I sent you. He will fill you in on the details of our problem.
3	line	Player	Alright, I'll get to it.
3	action	end
2	option	No.
3	line	Player	Actually, I've changed my mind.
3	line	Chancellor Hassan	I see. Well you know where to find me if you do wish to help us.
3	action	end
1	option	It's just too hot here. How can you stand it?
1	option	Do you mind if I just kill your warriors?
1	option	I'd better be off.
0	section	Talking to him again before meeting Osman
1	line	Chancellor Hassan	Hello again. Have you spoken to Osman yet? He should be just outside the palace.
1	line	Player	Not yet. I'll go and see him.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to him after meeting Osman
1	line	Chancellor Hassan	Hello again. I hear you have agreed to help rescue Prince Ali. On behalf of the Emir, I will have a reward ready for you upon your success.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Osman
1	line	Player	Osman? I was told by the Chancellor to come and speak to you. Apparently you have an issue that I can help with.
1	line	Osman	That would be an apt description. However, I find you to be an interesting choice by the Chancellor. Why has he chosen to trust you with this task over one of our own?
1	line	Player	Er... I just asked if he needed help and he said yes.
1	line	Osman	That man is far too trusting at a time when we must take extra care. However, if he has made his decision, I will not question it. Still, you should know that I will be keeping a close eye on you.
1	line	Player	Fair enough. So what is this issue?
1	line	Osman	Prince Ali, heir to the Emir of Al Kharid, has been taken. My spies have already discovered where he is being held, but we need someone to make the rescue.
1	line	Player	Well I'm sure I can manage that. How do I go about rescuing him?
1	line	Osman	The Prince has been taken by a group of bandits led by the self-proclaimed 'Lady' Keli. They are holding him in the abandoned jail just east of Draynor Village.
1	line	Osman	According to our information, Keli is the only one able to freely move around the area. For you to get the Prince out, you will need to disguise him as her. She will of course need dealing with first.
1	line	Player	Why can't I just go in and kill her and her bandits?
1	line	Osman	And endanger the life of the Prince in the process? No. There will be no unnecessary risks. We need to do this with as little bloodshed as possible.
1	line	Player	You make a fair point. Do you know what Keli looks like?
1	line	Osman	She has blonde hair and wears pink clothes. My daughter, Leela, one of my spies, is currently in Draynor Village keeping an eye on the jail. I'm sure she can help you with the specifics.
1	line	Osman	Before you go, there is one more thing. You'll need a key to get the Prince out of his cell. Keli has the only one. You could steal it, but that seems like a risk we should avoid.
1	line	Player	But if she has the only copy, and I can't just steal it, how do I get the key?
1	line	Osman	If you bring me an imprint of the key along with a bronze bar, I can show you how to make a copy. You should be able to make an imprint of the key using some soft clay.
1	line	Osman	Of course, you'll need to find a way to get Keli to show you the key without causing suspicion. I'm sure Leela can help you with that.
1	line	Player	Sounds like I should head on over to Draynor Village and see Leela then.
1	line	Osman	Indeed. Do you have any further questions before you go?
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	Do you know why they've taken the Prince?
2	line	Player	Do you know why they've taken the Prince?
2	line	Osman	No, but we have our theories.
2	line	Player	Care to share them?
2	line	Osman	No. You have not yet proven yourself enough to be trusted with that information.
2	line	Osman	Now, do you have any further questions?
2	action	other
1	option	Where abouts in Draynor is Leela?
2	line	Player	Where abouts in Draynor is Leela?
2	line	Osman	She will be somewhere near the abandoned jail that the bandits are using. It's just east of the village.
2	line	Osman	Do you have any further questions?
2	action	other
1	option	No. I think I know everything I need to.
2	line	Player	No. I think I know everything I need to.
2	line	Osman	Then you should get going.
2	action	end
