0	section	Talking to Leela
1	line	Player	You must be Leela. Your father sent me to help rescue Prince Ali.
1	line	Leela	Yes, he sent word ahead that you'd be coming. Are you aware of the plan?
1	line	Player	I need to obtain a copy of the key to the Prince's cell, create a disguise for him that makes him look like Keli and then break him out of the jail.
1	line	Leela	I'd say that's a good summary. Now, do you have any questions for me about any part of the plan?
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	Any ideas for the key?
2	line	Player	Any ideas for the key?
2	line	Leela	Keli keeps it on her at all times, on a chain around her neck. If you can convince her to show it to you, you might be able to use some soft clay to take an imprint.
2	cond	If the player hasn't obtained the key print yet:
3	line	Player	That doesn't sound easy.
3	line	Leela	My suggestion is that you pretend to be interested in joining her bandits. From there, you should be able to steer the conversation towards the key.
3	line	Leela	Once you have the imprint, take it to my father along with a bronze bar. He'll then be able to make us a copy.
3	action	continues
2	cond	If the player has the key print in their inventory:
3	line	Player	I already have the imprint!
3	line	Leela	Then you should take it to my father along with a bronze bar. He'll then be able to make us a copy.
3	action	continues
2	line	Leela	Do you have any other questions about the plan?
2	action	other
1	option	Any ideas for the disguise?
2	line	Player	Any ideas for the disguise?
2	line	Leela	To make the Prince look like Keli, you'll need a blonde wig and a pink skirt. You'll also want some skin paste to hide the black eye he got when they captured him.
2	line	Leela	There's an old sailor in the village who makes rope. Perhaps he could make you a wig. Don't forget to dye it once you have one.
2	line	Leela	For the skin paste, there's a local witch who's apparently an expert on all sorts of potions. I'm sure she could make you some. I hear she also sells dye, if you need some for the wig.
2	line	Leela	Finally there's the skirt. I imagine you could just buy one from any clothes shop. Thessalia's Fine Clothes in Varrock is probably the closest.
2	line	Leela	Do you have any other questions about the plan?
2	action	other
1	option	Don't think so. I'll go and prepare.
2	line	Player	Don't think so. I'll go and prepare.
2	action	end
