0	section	Talking to Joe
1	line	Player	Hi there.
1	line	Joe	What do you want?
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	I have some beer here. Fancy one?
2	line	Player	I have some beer here. Fancy one?
2	line	Joe	Ah, that would be lovely. Only one though, just to wet my throat.
2	line	Player	Of course. It must be tough being here without a drink.
2	box	You hand a beer to the guard. He drinks it in seconds.
2	line	Joe	That was perfect! I can't thank you enough.
2	line	Player	How are you? Still okay? Not too drunk?
2	cond	If the player has less than three beers:
3	line	Joe	No, I don't get drunk from only one drink. I reckon I'd need at least two more for that. Still, thanks for the beer.
3	action	end
2	cond	If the player has two more beers:
3	line	Player	Would you care for another beer, my friend?
3	line	Joe	I'd better not. I don't want to be drunk on duty.
3	line	Player	Here, just keep these for later. I hate to see a thirsty guard.
3	box	You hand two more beers to the guard. He takes a sip of one, and then he quickly drinks them both.
3	line	Joe	Franksh! That wash jusht what I need to shtay on guard. No more beersh, I don't want to get drunk.
3	action	end
1	option	Tell me about the life of a guard.
2	line	Player	Tell me about the life of a guard.
2	line	Joe	Well, the hours are good, but most of those hours are a drag.
2	line	Joe	Sometimes I wonder if I should have spent more time learning when I was a young boy. Maybe I wouldn't be here now, scared of Keli.
2	select	Select an Option
2	option	What did you want to be when you were a boy?
3	action	below
2	option	I'd better go.
3	action	below
1	option	What did you want to be when you were a boy?
2	line	Player	What did you want to be when you were a boy?
2	line	Joe	Well, I loved to sit by the lake, with my toes in the water. I'd shoot the fish with my bow and arrow.
2	line	Player	That's a strange hobby for a boy.
2	line	Joe	It kept us from goblin hunting, which was what most boys did.
2	line	Joe	Hang on... Why do you ask? What do you want?
2	select	Select an Option
2	option	Hey, chill out. I won't cause you trouble.
3	line	Player	Hey, chill out. I won't cause you trouble.
3	line	Joe	Sorry, it's hard to relax when I'm on duty. Stress of the job, and all.
3	line	Player	So why do you do it?
3	line	Joe	There's good money in it, and some of the shouting I rather like.
3	line	Joe	RESISTANCE IS USELESS!
3	select	Select an Option
3	option	So what do you buy with your great wages?
4	line	Player	So what do you buy with your great wages?
4	line	Joe	Really, after working here, there's only time for a drink or three. All us guards go to the same pub and drink ourselves stupid.
4	line	Joe	It's what I enjoy these days. I can't resist the sight of a really cold beer.
